\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces   Energy versus imaginary time $\tau $ for the TFI model using the imaginary-time TEBD algorithm. The energy converges to the ground state in the long-time limit. Calculations were performed with $N=30$ spins for three values of the time step $\eta $. Parameters are $h_Z=0$ and $h_X=1$. The maximum bond dimension used here is $\chi =40$ (relative precision better than $10^{-3}$), but $\chi =10$ is indistinguishable at the scale of the figure. The reference energy was obtained with the DMRG algorithm implemented using the TeNPy package \cite  {hauschild2018}. (Contributed by Chen-How Huang).}}{38}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tebd}{{3}{38}{Energy versus imaginary time $\tau $ for the TFI model using the imaginary-time TEBD algorithm. The energy converges to the ground state in the long-time limit. Calculations were performed with $N=30$ spins for three values of the time step $\eta $. Parameters are $h_Z=0$ and $h_X=1$. The maximum bond dimension used here is $\chi =40$ (relative precision better than $10^{-3}$), but $\chi =10$ is indistinguishable at the scale of the figure. The reference energy was obtained with the DMRG algorithm implemented using the TeNPy package \cite {hauschild2018}. (Contributed by Chen-How Huang)}{figure.caption.3}{}}
